// An 'extern system' declaration, and the symbol it lowers to.
//
// A characterisation scenario for the symbol-generation refactor: cases.toml
// pins today's spelling so that a change to how names are generated can show
// it did not move. 'system' selects the platform's system calling convention
// and imports the symbol from a DLL, which is what the IR line records.
//
// It compiles rather than runs because the one system routine every Windows
// build has, GetTickCount from kernel32, is not something the runner links
// against; the declaration is the whole subject, and the call is there only so
// the optimizer has a reason to keep it.

extern system fn GetTickCount() u32

fn ticks() u32 {
  GetTickCount()
}
